00:08:07.772 --> 00:08:10.554
(dark but also chill music)

00:08:11.216 --> 00:08:15.500
La Llorona’s curse follows three specific
steps: First, she burns the children with

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.960
her tears, by grabbing their arms and scorching
them.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:22.150
By doing this, she gains access to them, including
the ability to put them in a trance and lure

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.150
them to her.

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:27.103
This aspect of the legend would reflect her
own childrens’ trust in her before she drowned them.

00:08:27.103 --> 00:08:31.199
With all of her victims, her method of attack
is drowning in the nearest body of water.

00:08:31.199 --> 00:08:34.959
The location of the burn marks left on their
arms also ties back to the legend from the

00:08:34.959 --> 00:08:35.959
1600s.

00:08:35.959 --> 00:08:40.669
The burns are in a very visible spot, and
from what we can see, most or all of the families

00:08:40.669 --> 00:08:43.159
her spirit terrorizes are single mothers.

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:47.300
Children in single-parent households are significantly
more likely to be abused, according to this

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.430
study in the National Library of Medicine.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:53.339
As I mentioned, Patricia was already subject
to welfare checks before La Llorona entered

00:08:53.339 --> 00:08:54.339
her life.

00:08:54.339 --> 00:08:57.680
If abuse is found during a welfare check,
law enforcement may take away the children

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:58.779
for their safety.

00:08:58.779 --> 00:09:03.069
So the very visible burn marks feel like La
Llorona’s revenge, after her children were

00:09:03.069 --> 00:09:06.930
unfairly taken away from her; she’s imparting
that same pain onto her victims.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:09.480
This is exactly what happens to Patricia.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.060
Keeping the boys hidden away in the blessed
closet was her last hope at keeping Carlos

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:17.850
and Tomas safe from La Llorona, but during
her welfare check, Anna takes them out leaving

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.490
them completely vulnerable.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.449
As the boys sleep in the foster care institution,
La Llorona makes her next move.

00:09:23.449 --> 00:09:26.610
She puts Tomas in a trance and summons him
out of the bedroom.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:30.619
Carlos wakes up, and seeing his brother just
standing at the edge of the room, runs towards

00:09:30.619 --> 00:09:33.430
him, trying to get him to come back to bed,
but it’s too late.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:37.829
Carlos catches sight of La Llorona in the
mirror, then after her briefly disappearing,

00:09:37.829 --> 00:09:42.206
he gazes upon a puddle of water from a leak
in the ceiling, and this happens.

00:09:42.206 --> 00:09:43.248
– Carlos...

00:09:43.248 --> 00:09:44.117
(WAILING SCREAM)

00:09:44.117 --> 00:09:44.999
(WAILING SCREAM)
(Carlos screams)

00:09:44.999 --> 00:09:48.089
– She grabs both of them and takes them to the
nearby river to drown them.

00:09:48.089 --> 00:09:52.249
Anna is called to the crime scene to identify
the bodies and with no father to watch them,

00:09:52.249 --> 00:09:55.609
has no choice but to take her own children
with and lock them in the car.

00:09:55.609 --> 00:09:57.119
– Stay in the car, OK?

00:09:57.119 --> 00:09:59.240
And please don’t wake up your sister.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:03.319
– But Chris is a kid, and of course, kids don’t
listen to their parents, especially when they’re

00:10:03.319 --> 00:10:05.999
right next to an active crime scene that looks
really cool!

00:10:05.999 --> 00:10:10.500
Patricia also shows up and, driven mad with
grief, tries to blame Anna for interfering.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.519
When Anna asks what she’s talking about,
Patricia tells her:

00:10:13.519 --> 00:10:14.800
– La Llorona.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.779
– At this point, Patricia essentially becomes
a proxy of La Llorona herself.

00:10:18.779 --> 00:10:22.901
She prayed to wicked spirit, asking her to
take Anna’s children in place of her own.

00:10:22.901 --> 00:10:26.860
–... and I prayed to her,
to give my children back to me and take yours instead!

00:10:26.860 --> 00:10:31.779
– Patricia is now following La Llorona’s ghastly
footsteps, hoping to sacrifice other children

00:10:31.779 --> 00:10:33.679
in order to trade their souls for her own.

00:10:33.679 --> 00:10:37.970
It’s almost as though the spirit La Llorona
sees Anna’s kids through Patricia, because

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.639
Anna’s kids aren’t targetted until Patricia
makes eye contact with Chris as she’s taken

00:10:41.639 --> 00:10:42.999
away in a police car.

00:10:42.999 --> 00:10:46.249
When Chris ignores his mother’s warning
and gets out of the car to investigate, La

00:10:46.249 --> 00:10:50.139
Llorona sobs in a nearby alley, luring Chris
to her sound.

00:10:50.139 --> 00:10:54.499
As he checks to see if she’s okay, her head
suddenly snaps in his direction and she lunges

00:10:54.499 --> 00:10:58.029
toward him, allowing herself to burn him with
her tears by grabbing his arm and scorching

00:10:58.029 --> 00:10:59.029
it.

00:10:59.029 --> 00:11:00.430
She’s now attached herself to the family.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:04.120
She chases him back to the car, where he breaks
the other rule that Anna set for him, not

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.569
to wake up his sister, as he begs to be let
back in.

00:11:06.569 --> 00:11:10.819
Only he can see La Llorona screeching at him
on the other side of the window, but Chris’s

00:11:10.819 --> 00:11:12.730
behavior is still enough to scare her.

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.949
In addition to that, Samantha becomes La Llorona’s
next target.

00:11:15.949 --> 00:11:19.259
The following day, while Anna is at work,
she’s playing out in the rain with a see

00:11:19.259 --> 00:11:20.259
through umbrella.

00:11:20.259 --> 00:11:25.034
La Llorona attempts to lure her in, the same
way she did with Chris by crying off in the distance.

00:11:25.034 --> 00:11:29.720
However, Sam has more self-preservation and
stops at the fence at the end of their yard,

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.850
so La Llorona resorts to other tactics.

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.249
She blows Sam’s umbrella into the water,
and when she reaches out to get it, she’s

00:11:35.249 --> 00:11:37.159
met with a surprise.

00:11:37.159 --> 00:11:39.818
(high-pitched scream)

00:11:40.889 --> 00:11:45.190
She too is burned when La Llorona grabs her
arm and scorches it with her tears.

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:49.089
That night, she puts Chris into a heavy trance,
and Anna finds him repeatedly opening and

00:11:49.089 --> 00:11:50.329
closing the front door.

00:11:50.329 --> 00:11:54.029
She thinks he’s sleepwalking, but he’s
really setting the stage for La Llorona to

00:11:54.029 --> 00:11:57.579
blow open the door, granting her access to
the house, which she uses to confront Anna

00:11:57.579 --> 00:11:58.930
that same night.

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:02.779
– Get out of my house!

00:12:02.779 --> 00:12:03.779
– Mom?

00:12:03.779 --> 00:12:06.939
–  [Zac] Anna ushers the kids to come in and sleep
in her bed, while staying up all night on

00:12:06.939 --> 00:12:08.209
guard with a baseball bat.

00:12:08.209 --> 00:12:10.119
The terror continues the next day.

00:12:10.119 --> 00:12:14.160
While Anna is at work, La Llorona lures Chris
into Samantha’s bedroom, knocks him to the

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:18.269
floor with another powerful gust of supernatural
wind, and lunges for him, scaring him away

00:12:18.269 --> 00:12:22.250
to the edge of the stairs, which she pushes
him down after appearing in the adjacent room.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:25.850
He lands on his wrist just before Anna walks
through the door and she completely

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:29.519
overreacts, considering from her point of
view, he was just sitting there with a sprained

00:12:29.519 --> 00:12:30.519
wrist.

00:12:30.519 --> 00:12:31.519
– CHRIS!

00:12:31.519 --> 00:12:32.519
CHRIS!!

00:12:32.519 --> 00:12:37.089
– Sure, La Llorona probably could have killed
Chris right then and there if she wanted to,

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:40.790
but she may have been setting Anna up, just
like she did to Patricia, to seem like an

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:44.519
ill equipped mother, as she would know first
hand that having her own children taken away

00:12:44.519 --> 00:12:46.620
from her was a pain worse than death.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.749
The ensuing social services visit at Anna’s
home was probably a humiliation very much

00:12:50.749 --> 00:12:55.439
akin to La Llorona’s feelings when the conquistador
she married took her boys away to a “better

00:12:55.439 --> 00:12:56.439
suited” woman.

00:12:56.439 --> 00:12:59.870
Also, La Llorona still needs to burn Anna
with the black tears in order to complete

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:00.870
the curse.

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:05.439
As Samantha is upstairs taking a bath alone,
which seems like kinda not a good idea, given

00:13:05.439 --> 00:13:09.500
everything that has happened, La Llorona seizes
the opportunity to attack her and bring Anna

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.230
to a place of vulnerability.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:15.029
Samantha is washing her hair with her eyes
closed when she feels a pair of hands massaging

00:13:15.029 --> 00:13:16.029
her scalp.

00:13:16.029 --> 00:13:19.949
For a brief moment, La Llorona is tender with
Samantha, just as she likely was with her

00:13:19.949 --> 00:13:21.029
own children.

00:13:21.029 --> 00:13:23.589
Sam is tricked by the feeling of that motherly
touch.

00:13:23.589 --> 00:13:27.980
However, as she leans her head back to rinse,
La Llorona’s decrepit hands pull her under

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.000
and pin her there.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.910
Anna and Chris hear the commotion in the bathroom
and run up to save her, just in time.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:36.720
Anna pulls her out of the tub where she crawls
backwards in petrified fear, almost looking

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:40.943
as though she’s scared of her mother, but
actually gazing on to La Llorona.

00:13:40.943 --> 00:13:44.439
This time it’s Anna’s turn to get burned
by The Weeping Woman’s touch, just as she

00:13:44.439 --> 00:13:45.899
turns around to see her

00:13:45.899 --> 00:13:49.589
By this point, La Llorona has marked each
family member to complete the curse and can

00:13:49.589 --> 00:13:52.339
now strike at any moment to kill the children.

00:13:52.339 --> 00:13:57.359
Things would be complicated, however, when
Anna goes outside the church to bring in reinforcements.

00:13:57.359 --> 00:14:01.073
(impact, but slightly different than the one before)

00:14:02.639 --> 00:14:06.440
(morbid music)

00:14:06.749 --> 00:14:11.160
Anna and the kids seek out the currendero
Rafael, who reluctantly agrees and implements

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:15.189
him unorthodox methods by having Anna and
kids roll eggs all over everything in the

00:14:15.189 --> 00:14:16.189
house.

00:14:16.189 --> 00:14:20.311
He calls the ritual La Limpa and says that
it’s meant to detect evil in the house.

00:14:20.311 --> 00:14:23.899
The ritual of rolling an egg in its shell
to pick up or ward off evil is a practice

00:14:23.899 --> 00:14:27.929
that not only goes way back in Mexican healing
but it is still in practice today.

00:14:27.929 --> 00:14:32.049
He cracks one egg in a bowl revealing the
yolk to have turned to a burning black tar,

00:14:32.049 --> 00:14:36.740
and the other eggs explode, gushing the substance
everywhere, almost like the spiritual equivalent

00:14:36.740 --> 00:14:41.230
of a paper towel picking up dirt from a surface,
it reveals that La Llorona has definitely

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.459
made her mark on the house and the family.

00:14:43.459 --> 00:14:47.480
Anna and the children assist Rafael in several
other rituals leaving the house looking very

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:51.279
similar to how Patricia’s looked when Anna
went to pay her that initial welfare check.

00:14:51.279 --> 00:14:55.529
While doing this, Chris notices Rafael’s
cross, which he explains to be crafted from

00:14:55.529 --> 00:14:59.999
the fire trees that surround the river where
La Llorona drowned her children.

00:14:59.999 --> 00:15:06.139
– They say, the fire trees wept as La Llorona
drowned her children.

00:15:06.139 --> 00:15:10.970
As the only witness to her sins, they hold
a special power over her.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:14.680
– He also reveals the vial of La Llorona’s
black blood tears, which he collected from

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:15.680
Patricia’s house.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.470
He mixes it with Holy water and refers to
it as “antivenom”.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:22.689
La Llorona arrives later that night, viscous
and determined to find the children.

00:15:22.689 --> 00:15:26.249
Anna and the kids believe they’re being
protected as they’re surrounded by candles,

00:15:26.249 --> 00:15:30.470
huddled in the living room, under Rafael’s
direction, but La Llorona takes her by surprise

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:33.951
as she whales out a horrible sound that extinguishes
all of the lights.

00:15:33.951 --> 00:15:37.320
(aforementioned horrible sound)

00:15:40.089 --> 00:15:43.629
Anna and the kids are actually exactly where
La Llorona wants them.

00:15:43.629 --> 00:15:48.129
It wouldn’t be a movie in the Conjurverse
if there weren’t some air yeeting and La

00:15:48.129 --> 00:15:49.339
Llorona starts that here.

00:15:49.339 --> 00:15:52.709
Anna is air yeeted out of the way and left
unconscious on the floor.

00:15:52.709 --> 00:15:57.350
As the kids beg Rafael for help he does nothing
but instead slinks back into the shadows of

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:01.560
the house, leaving the kids unprotected and
completely susceptible to be air yeeted.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:05.199
When Anna comes to, she gets up to try and
save her son, but she’s not going to make

00:16:05.199 --> 00:16:06.199
it in time.

00:16:06.199 --> 00:16:10.239
At just the last possible moment, Rafael sticks
a hand out and grabs Chris while throwing

00:16:10.239 --> 00:16:13.059
his vial of his “antivenom” into La Llorona’s
face.

00:16:13.059 --> 00:16:17.220
This has the desired effect and burns her
face so badly that she lets go of Chris and

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:20.060
Rafael is able to shove her out of the house
through the front door.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:23.579
He slams it shut, and puts down another row
of seeds from the fire tree.

00:16:23.579 --> 00:16:27.589
Explained another way, it was all a setup
to lock La Llorona out of the house, and to

00:16:27.589 --> 00:16:29.709
her frustration, she fell for it.

00:16:29.709 --> 00:16:33.679
Because the seeds are collected from the same
fire tree that the cross is made from, La

00:16:33.679 --> 00:16:36.699
Llorona cross this barrier, as long as the
line is not broken.

00:16:36.699 --> 00:16:40.579
And apparently she can’t use any of that
supernatural wind power to break them herself.

00:16:40.579 --> 00:16:41.999
I don’t make the rules!

00:16:41.999 --> 00:16:46.399
I guess Rafa overlooked the Garcia’s back
door though, because La Llorona promptly uses

00:16:46.399 --> 00:16:47.889
her force to blow it up.

00:16:47.889 --> 00:16:52.620
Anna, Chris and Rafael race back to seal it
shut but Rafael was not the only one playing

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.679
chess here, this was also just a clever distraction.

00:16:55.679 --> 00:16:56.959
– Clever girl.

00:16:56.959 --> 00:17:01.149
– She’s really just using the back door as
a diversion to trick Samantha into breaking

00:17:01.149 --> 00:17:02.149
the seal.

00:17:02.149 --> 00:17:05.810
La Llorona gets ahold of Misty, Samantha’s
beloved doll that she associates with her

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:06.850
deceased father.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:10.919
She would not be the first or last evil entity
to manipulate a doll in the Conjurverse.

00:17:10.919 --> 00:17:15.000
Misty is set outside, just barely out of Samantha’s
reach, so she’d have to reach out past the

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.000
seeds to get it.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:19.000
It’s also fitting that she uses this doll
named Misty.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:23.149
Mist is the gaseous form of water, and water
is La Llorona’s murder weapon.

00:17:23.149 --> 00:17:26.799
Samantha takes the bait and is just barely
able to get Misty without breaking the line

00:17:26.799 --> 00:17:31.610
of seeds, but Anna sees her at the last second
and yells at her to get away from the door,

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:35.490
causing her to get distracted and accidentally
drag the doll through the line of seeds, granting

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.120
La Llorona access to the house.

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:41.860
La Llorona immediately grabs Sam for one of
the most dramatic air yeeting sequences yet.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:45.850
She takes her to the nearest body of water,
the backyard pool and holds her under.

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:48.740
Anna dives in and feverishly searches with
a flashlight.

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:52.770
Upon finding her at the bottom, La Llorona
attacks Anna, and during the scuffle, Anna

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:56.710
rips off La Llorona’s necklace; the same
necklace given to her by her boys that she

00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:58.289
said she would wear forever.

00:17:58.289 --> 00:18:03.700
This absolutely enrages La Llorona, it’s
the last connection she has to her own children.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:08.370
But before she can retaliate, Rafael blesses
the water and mixes in salt, causing the pool

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.510
water to be turned into Holy water, which
drives La Llorona out.

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:14.690
Anna is able to rescue Samantha from drowning,
but just like Tomas, Samantha is now in a

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:19.360
trance just like what Patricia’s son Tomas
experienced shortly before his death.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:23.760
Rafael and Anna realize that the only way
to keep Samantha from just walking outside

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:27.950
into La Llorona’s grasp again is that they
must keep her locked away, the same method

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:31.100
that Patricia was reprimanded for the night
of Anna’s visit.

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:36.105
So fittingly, Patricia would be La Llorona’s
last trump card to weaponize against Anna’s family. 

00:18:36.105 --> 00:18:41.070
Being a regular corporeal human, Patricia
has no problem simply walking over the fire

00:18:41.070 --> 00:18:43.080
seed barrier to abduct Chris and Samantha.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.700
– [Patricia] You took my babies from me.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.320
She’ll give them back to me.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:50.830
– [Zac] Patricia shoots Rafael in the shoulder and
breaks the line of seeds at the door, allowing

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:52.200
La Llorona to get inside.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:56.630
It isn’t completely clear if Patricia entered
Anna’s house on her own volition, or if

00:18:56.630 --> 00:19:00.500
it was under La Llorona’s direction, but
in either case, we know she was manipulated

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:03.830
by her belief that her children’s souls
could be freed if she offered the souls of

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.580
Anna’s children in their stead.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.029
La Llorona, after powering her way through
everyone into the house, tosses Anna into

00:19:09.029 --> 00:19:10.279
the basement stairway.

00:19:10.279 --> 00:19:14.010
As she is thrown, she drops La Llorona’s
necklace, but Chris picks it up and keeps

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.010
it close.

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:18.880
At this point the trance on Samantha is broken
with no explanation as to why.

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:22.770
I would speculate that it could be tied to
the sunrise, a symbol of the passage of time

00:19:22.770 --> 00:19:23.970
into the next day.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:27.181
Again, this goes back to the idea that Patricia
brought up way back at the beginning: that

00:19:27.181 --> 00:19:31.120
she only needed to keep her family safe a
little longer, and then the evil would potentially

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.120
move on.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:36.050
The children run to the attic, but the Bawlin’
Broad finds and corners them.

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:40.000
As the final moments draw near and she walks
towards them, Chris uses his last

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:42.360
line of defense, La Llorona’s necklace.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.029
This causes her anger to suddenly disappear.

00:19:45.029 --> 00:19:48.840
Her face returns to the soft, kind features
from her natural life.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:51.784
Different people are going to interpret this
in different ways, but I think in that

00:19:51.784 --> 00:19:56.440
moment La Llorona saw Chris as one of her
own children, offering the necklace, and anger

00:19:56.440 --> 00:20:00.659
and malice temporarily went away, allowing
her to take on the appearance of more of a

00:20:00.659 --> 00:20:01.659
friendly ghost.

00:20:01.659 --> 00:20:05.419
On the contrary, you could look at it as another
one of her tricks – her trying to get the

00:20:05.419 --> 00:20:07.190
Garcia children to let their guard down.

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:11.350
The moment of pleasantness would be short
lived, however, as Samantha accidentally uncovers

00:20:11.350 --> 00:20:16.590
a mirror, allowing La Llorona sees the reflection
of her true monstrous self, eyes covered in

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:19.860
black blood, and she immediately reverts to her
previous form.

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:24.049
This moment did buy Chris and Samantha just
enough time for Anna and Rafael to reach the

00:20:24.049 --> 00:20:25.269
attic and protect them.

00:20:25.269 --> 00:20:29.059
La Llorona turns her attention to Rafael,
because he poses the biggest threat with his

00:20:29.059 --> 00:20:31.409
cross made from the fire tree seeds.

00:20:31.409 --> 00:20:33.960
She vehemently throws him into a pile of boxes.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:37.980
With all of the Garcia family together now,
she charges them, however, Rafael is just

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:42.039
able to kick his the cross across the room
to Anna who grabs it and promptly stabs La

00:20:42.039 --> 00:20:43.601
Llorona through the chest.

00:20:43.601 --> 00:20:47.391
(La Llorona screams as she decomposes)

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:54.419
And that would conclude the Garcia family’s
chapter with the malicious Central American

00:20:54.419 --> 00:20:55.000
legend.

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:55.705
However!

00:20:55.705 --> 00:20:58.467
This might not be the final chapter of her
story.

00:20:58.467 --> 00:21:02.509
After Anna and the kids say goodbye to Rafael
later that morning, she looks back into a

00:21:02.509 --> 00:21:06.606
puddle and sees something that alarms her
while we hear the sounds of children’s laughter.

00:21:06.606 --> 00:21:11.751
(laughter)

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:16.350
Could this be the the return of La Llorona,
who was always associated with water, or does

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:20.880
the youthful laughter suggest that a new entity,
perhaps one of her victims has legendized

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:25.929
as a new threat, joining the likes of Bathsheba,
Malthus, Valak, and Isla among many other

00:21:25.929 --> 00:21:27.539
evil beings in the Conjurverse.

00:21:27.539 --> 00:21:32.130
There is a lot more to learn about these antagonists,
so check out that playlist on the left for

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:35.370
the low-down on the Conjurverse’s most horrifying
villains.

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:39.260
And remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week, ring the deathbell

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:43.470
and select ALL notifications and I will see
you in the next one.

00:21:43.470 --> 00:21:45.801
Assuming we both survive.

00:21:47.942 --> 00:21:50.145
– [Velma] Jinkies, that's impressive!

